<</Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/Alt (Architecture of an experiment control system A control PC sends compiled sequences over Ethernet to a real-time core that holds the clock. The core drives TTL, DDS, DAC and AWG output cards and reads ADC, counter and camera inputs. The outputs go through AOM drivers, coil drivers and shutters to the atoms; detectors return signals to the inputs. Slow instruments such as wavemeters and synthesizers connect to the PC directly.)
/P 8036 0 R
/Pg 673 0 R
/K 7>>
